  "$comment": "Runtime caps original UTF-8 at 1 MiB, nesting at 128 containers, and each number token at 128 bytes. Rejects duplicate/unknown fields, trailing data, nonfinite values, nonzero-decimal underflow-to-zero, and integer tags/sense in float notation. Arrays are bounded during decode before the excess element. JSON Schema cannot express raw token/byte constraints, UTF-8 metadata byte lengths, exact f64 arithmetic, inertia conditioning, axis spacing/products, coupled component/initial-state containment, energy/actuator-disk inequalities or actual atmosphere/wind/inflow support. Use the exact loader and runtime as the final admission gates."
